This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The conversation is a continuation focused on **creating LVGL graphical cards for Agent replies** on the openvela embedded platform (qemu-arm64-v8a-ap now, real device later). The user previously selected "enhanced bubble cards" (keep chat bubble layout but render Agent replies as richer cards with title bar/divider/status color bar).

   The immediate flow this session:
   - User showed a screenshot (Image #9) saying "你自己看" (look yourself), wanting me to diagnose why the interface wasn't done well.
   - After I diagnosed (CJK tofu + invisible card boundary) and rebuilt, user confirmed via AskUserQuestion: **"有窗口,但中文还是豆腐块"** (window present, but Chinese still tofu blocks).
   - The core intent: make Agent reply text (Chinese) actually render legibly as cards on the qemu visualization. The earlier explicit requirement still in effect: "在ask是，要显示在可视化界面上" (ask command replies must display on the visualization interface, not only when ai_agent starts).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - LVGL v9.1.0 (v9 API), NuttX LVGL port (`lv_nuttx_init`, `lv_is_initialized()`, loop thread with `lv_timer_handler()`)
   - LVGL built-in fonts: `lv_font_montserrat_14` (Latin only), `lv_font_simsun_16_cjk` (1272-char subset, misses common simplified chars like 这/个/态/经/办/张)
   - LVGL `LV_USE_TINY_TTF` — stb_truetype port, no external FreeType library. API: `lv_tiny_ttf_create_file(path, font_size)`, `lv_tiny_ttf_create_data(data, size, font_size)`, `lv_tiny_ttf_destroy()`. Header `lv_tiny_ttf.h` included by lvgl.h line 135 under `LV_USE_TINY_TTF`.
   - `tiny_ttf_create_file` uses `lv_fs_open`/`lv_fs_read`/`lv_fs_seek` (keeps file stream open, reads during rasterization) — CRASHED (data abort) on qemu
   - `tiny_ttf_create_data` — in-memory buffer, no file I/O during render (safer)
   - LVGL filesystem: `LV_FS_POSIX_LETTER=47` ('/'), `LV_FS_POSIX_PATH="/"`. Path `"/data/data/font/..."` resolves via POSIX driver.
   - MiSans-Regular.ttf (2.5MB, full simplified Chinese coverage) at `vendor/openvela/boards/vela/resource/font/MiSans-Regular.ttf`
   - openvela build system: `source build/envsetup.sh && lunch <boardpath> <bindir> && m -j8` OR `./build.sh <boardpath> --cmake -j8`. cmake configure cmd (envsetup line 679): `cmake -B $BIN -S $T/nuttx -DBOARD_CONFIG=$VELA_BUILD_BOARD_CONFIG -DCUSTOM_MODULE_PATH=$T/build/cmake -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache -DEXTRA_FLAGS=$VELA_EXTRA_FLAGS -GNinja`
   - `_do_cmake_generator` (envsetup) only runs cmake configure if `[ ! -d CMAKE_BINARY_DIR ]` (directory existence, NOT CMakeCache presence) — key gotcha
   - `m`/`ninja` regenerate .config from defconfig only when .config is MISSING (delete .config to reseed)
   - vela_data.bin built by `mcopy -i vela_data.bin -sv <board>/prebuilts/data/ ::` — mcopy copies dir CONTENTS into a subdir named after the dir, so prebuilts/data/font/X → image ::/data/font/X → NuttX /data/data/font/X. gen_images target depends only on `nuttx`, NOT on prebuilts/data contents (must rm vela_data.bin to force regen).
   - rc.sysinit: `mount -t fatfs /dev/virtblk1 /data` (data FAT image mounts at /data)
   - QEMU display: only `none` and `sdl` backends (NOT gtk). SDL window works for user but I can't capture via X11 (no window manager, xwd BadColor). Use `-display sdl -serial mon:stdio` in tmux with trailing `; sleep 30` to keep session alive.
